      "title": "A Letter from the Secretariat of State",
      "body": "The letter comes to {@bishop} first, on the letterhead of the Secretariat of State, and {@bishop} sends it on to you with a note of his own clipped to the corner. {curia_offer} would like a priest of the diocese as an official for five years: a desk, a residence near the Borgo, the files. {@bishop} writes that he can spare you, which is not quite true, and that nobody says no to this letter, which is. Men lent to Rome come home different, and some of them do not come home. The note ends: think about it, and then say yes.",
